From 817b31573448f2375280003906995297c99725f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yin Li <kevinli.ai.work@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 17 Sep 2026 22:23:18 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] [Frontend] Add return_token_logprobs to
 /inference/v1/generate

RL rollout collectors need one float per generated token: the sampled
token's (processed) logprob. On the token-in/token-out endpoint that
currently means logprobs=0 and parsing choices[].logprobs.content[i].logprob,
and on the server it means building a dict[int, Logprob] per position in
the output processor and a ChatCompletionLogProbsContent Pydantic object
per token in the frontend before JSON encoding. On an 8-core host serving
Qwen2.5-0.5B on one L20 (128 x 256-token rollouts, concurrency 64) that
per-token work is ~40 us/token of API-server CPU and takes throughput from
18.6K tok/s (no logprobs) to 13.7K (logprobs=0); --skip-tokenizer-init
does not change it, so it is object construction, not detokenization.

This adds GenerateRequest.return_token_logprobs. When set, the request
uses the engine's existing flat_logprobs representation and the response
carries choices[].token_logprobs: list[float], read directly from
FlatLogprobs.logprobs at each position's start index (the sampled token
is stored first). With logprobs unset it defaults to 0 and the OpenAI-style
logprobs object is omitted; with logprobs > 0 both are returned. Streaming
is rejected with a 400 (the per-chunk shape is a separate decision).

Same workload: 13.5K -> 16.6K tok/s (0.73x -> 0.89x of no-logprobs); with
--return-sampling-mask, the rollout contract (mask + token logprob) goes
from 11.8K to 14.0K tok/s on the 0.5B model and from 0.94x to 0.98x of
plain generation on Qwen3-4B. Values are identical to the object path
(max abs diff 0.0 over 16 seeded sequences under VLLM_BATCH_INVARIANT=1).

Tests: flat array equals the object path's per-token logprob, defaulting
of logprobs, coexistence with logprobs > 0, stream rejection.
